<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<TcPlcObject Version="1.1.0.1" ProductVersion="3.1.4024.12">
  <POU Name="F_GasManifold_ILK" Id="{3f1a5d70-0b2c-4d51-9a64-7c11e2b90a02}" SpecialFunc="None">
    <Declaration><![CDATA[(*
    F_GasManifold_ILK - site interlock permit for FB_GasManifold.

    PURPOSE
        Single home for every interlock condition that permits the
        sample-delivery gas manifold to drive its seven NC sample valves.

    USAGE
        Evaluated by the deployment that owns the manifold and wired into
        FB_GasManifold.i_xILK. FB_GasManifold is a reusable device block and
        never evaluates (nor forces) a permit itself: it propagates whatever
        this function returns to every one of its valve structures.

    OBJECTIVES
        - Replace the previous unconditional 'xILK := TRUE' inside the manifold
          block with an explicit, reviewable site condition.
        - Fail safe: an unhealthy gas manifold EtherCAT node returns FALSE, so
          every valve is held closed (these are normally-open valves whose DO
          closes them).
        - Keep the condition in one function so it can be reviewed and tested
          without instantiating the manifold.

    HISTORY
        2026-11-27 / Scirix Agent
            Function created while removing the hard-coded TRUE permit from
            FB_GasManifold (audit finding #505, convention conv_0121ae615346).
*)
FUNCTION F_GasManifold_ILK : BOOL
VAR_INPUT
    i_xPanelFieldbusOK : BOOL; // Gas manifold EtherCAT sync unit healthy (ST_M3DeviceBaseIO.i_SyncUnitWC)
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
    <Implementation>
      <ST><![CDATA[(* The manifold may only drive its valves while its EtherCAT sync unit is
   alive, otherwise the valve DOs and readbacks cannot be trusted. *)
F_GasManifold_ILK := i_xPanelFieldbusOK;]]></ST>
    </Implementation>
  </POU>
</TcPlcObject>
